{
  "Panes side by side or one under the other, as many as needed, with a handle between each two that the pointer drags and the keys move. A handle resizes the two panes beside it; a pane may be hidden from its handle, and may hold another splitter. For two panes with one fixed, see [SplitContainer](/layout).": "",
  "Pixels, shares and the rest": "",
  "Each `SplitPane` says its `size`: pixels stay pixels when the splitter changes size, a share (`'30%'`) divides the room the shares get, and a pane without a size takes an equal part of what is left. `minSize` and `maxSize` hold the handles. Drag a handle, or focus it and use the arrow keys, Home and End.": "",
  "Hiding a pane": "",
  "A `collapsible` pane gets a button on the handle next to it; Enter on the handle and a double press do the same. The neighbours take its room, and it comes back where it was. `onCollapsing` may refuse, `onCollapsed` tells.": "",
  "One inside another": "",
  "A pane is a `Panel`: put a `Splitter` of the other `orientation` in it for an editor over an output, next to a tree.": "",
  "After every move the panes’ pixels are written to `x-model` (and `onResized` tells). Give them back as `sizes` to restore a layout; `null` starts from the panes’ own sizes again.": "",
  "Each handle that can move or hide a pane is a stop, between the panes it lies between.": "",
  "Left and Right (Up and Down one under the other) move the handle by `step` pixels, within the panes’ least and most sizes; the other way round in a right-to-left page.": "",
  "Give the pane before the handle its least, or its most.": "",
  "Hides the pane before the handle, or shows it again; when that pane cannot be hidden, the one after.": "",
  "A `separator` named “Resize” in the kit language, with `aria-controls` on the pane before it, `aria-orientation`, and `aria-valuenow` as that pane’s share of the two beside the handle.": "",
  "Buttons named “Hide the pane” and “Show the pane”, out of the Tab order: Enter on the handle does the same.": "",
  "Out of sight and `inert`; focus inside it moves to the handle.": "",
  "A pane with a `text` is a `region` of that name.": "",
  "The splitter. `data-orientation`, `data-dragging` while a handle is dragged.": "",
  "A pane (a `Panel`). `data-collapsed` while hidden.": "",
  "A handle. `data-resizable`, `data-dragging`.": "",
  "The grip in the middle of a handle, the fold buttons at either end of it (`data-side`), their arrows.": "",
  "Units: the handle (`focus`), the line along it (`active`, `disabled`), the grip (`active`, `disabled`), the fold buttons (`hover`, `pressed`, `focus`) and their arrows, a pane (`collapsed`).": "",
  "The handle’s thickness, the line’s, the line’s under the pointer, the grip’s size.": "",
  "Splitter props": "",
  "`horizontal`: the panes side by side; `vertical`: one under the other.": "",
  "The handles can be dragged and moved with the keys (a pane’s own `resizable` wins).": "",
  "Every pane can be hidden from the handle next to it (a pane’s own `collapsible` wins).": "",
  "Pixels an arrow key moves a handle.": "",
  "The panes’ sizes in pane order (pixels, a share or `null`); given, they take the place of the panes’ own `size`. After a drag or a key the pixels are written to `x-model`.": "",
  "SplitPane props": "",
  "Pixels, a share (`'30%'`) of the room the shares divide, or `null` for an equal share of what is left.": "",
  "The least and the most it gets, in pixels.": "",
  "The handles next to it can hide it; `undefined` follows the splitter.": "",
  "Hidden, the neighbours taking its room.": "",
  "The handles next to it can change its size.": "",
  "Names the pane; the JSX `key` is read too.": "",
  "Content made with the pane, besides the JSX children.": "",
  "as `Panel`": "",
  "A pane is a `Panel`: its padding, its own scrolling, a frame, a name (a region).": "",
  "A handle is being dragged (`handle`, `sizes` in pixels).": "",
  "A drag ended or a key moved a handle (`handle`, `sizes`).": "",
  "A pane is about to be hidden or shown again (`pane`, `index`, `collapsed`, `byUser`); `cancel = true` leaves it.": "",
  "A pane was hidden or shown again.": "",
  "The panes in order, hidden ones too.": "",
  "The panes’ pixels along the split now; 0 for a hidden pane.": "",
  "Adds a pane at the end or at an index.": "",
  "Removes a pane and disposes it.": "",
  "Hides a pane (by index or the pane itself), or shows it again; `onCollapsing` is asked first. A pane’s own `collapse()` and `expand()` do the same.": ""
}
